== fm-claude-account-quota
ok - exhausted, 0%, missing, and unreadable accounts print facts and uncertainty without a verdict
ok - projected exhaustion prints usableRunwaySeconds and confidence
ok - a rate-limited account reports the vendor's own state and error
ok - ordinary and token:<file> accounts are measured in isolation, cached safely, and never leak the token
ok - an unusable token file is disclosed uncertainty and never read
ok - Keychain-kept roots are measured without the file-only flag and without an ambient token
ok - absent or malformed lists refuse before any read, and missing quota-axi reports in-band uncertainty
# all fm-claude-account-quota tests passed
exit=
== fm-worker-account
warning: re-init: ignored --initial-branch=main
ok - a list never chooses a secondmate's account: it needs its own pin and refuses --account
ok - both healthy: selects the declared Claude account with higher usable headroom and records account + reason
ok - one low: skips an account below the low-headroom threshold (default 20% or configured) and chooses the healthy account
ok - both low: emits a clear warning and keeps today's pinned-account fallback
ok - measurement unavailable keeps the candidate account eligible with disclosed uncertainty
ok - explicit --account overrides automatic selection, and malformed pool or threshold files refuse before launch
# all fm-worker-account tests passed
exit=
== fm-dispatch-resolve
ok - account: a claude profile passes its account to the profile line; bad or non-claude accounts do not
ok - shared-quota opt-out: no quota snapshot, deterministic declared-order pick, opt-out stated on every candidate
ok - shared-quota bypasses an unmet rule-level floor: the rule's own profile wins with no quota call
ok - shared-quota bypasses an unmet profile-level floor: the first declared profile wins with no quota call
ok - shared-quota keeps preferred_provider narrowing: the preferred family wins in declared order with no quota call
ok - shared_quota false keeps the unchanged quota-ranked behavior
ok - config/claude-accounts: per-account headroom feeds candidate and rule-floor evaluation, skips low accounts, and keeps unmeasured accounts eligible
# all fm-dispatch-resolve tests passed
exit=
== fm-control-relaunch
ok - fm-spawn --relaunch: a recorded worktree that is the primary home refuses
ok - fm-spawn --relaunch: a recorded worktree that is the project primary checkout refuses
ok - fm-spawn --relaunch: inherited Git overrides do not hide the project primary checkout
ok - fm-control relaunch: a worker with nothing to work from is never launched
ok - fm-control relaunch: a refusal before the agent is stopped leaves the durable record untouched
ok - fm-control relaunch: checkpoint inspection failures refuse before stopping
ok - fm-control relaunch: a launch failure after the stop keeps the prior record and reports the real state
ok - fm-control relaunch: unpublished rollback keeps concurrent durable metadata
exit=
